To close your account, return the ONT device and its power adapter within 14 days. If you keep the ONT, a fee of ₹2,500 applies, and a ₹1,500 fee applies for any mesh extender not returned. Your security deposit of ₹1,000 will be refunded within 7 days after we receive the equipment.  

Source: Account Closure Policy.", "latency_ms": 806.56, "tokens_used": 542, "prompt_tokens": 294, "completion_tokens": 248}

{"tool": "generate_ticket_reply", "reply": "[Ticket #T073]  
A solid (non‑flashing) orange LED means the ONT is either in firmware‑update mode or detecting a degraded optical signal (approximately –27 dBm to –30 dBm). Please wait about 10 minutes; if the light stays orange, try a single power‑cycle of the device.  

*Source: Troubleshooting – solid orange LED indicates firmware update mode or degraded optical signal.*", "latency_ms": 1103.01, "tokens_used": 541, "prompt_tokens": 276, "completion_tokens": 265}

{"tool": "generate_ticket_reply", "reply": "[Ticket #T118]  
I understand how frustrating a 2‑day outage can be. According to our Refund Policy, full plan refunds are only available within the first 30 days of activation, and your service has been active for three months, so a full refund isn’t applicable. However, outages that exceed 24 consecutive hours qualify for a pro‑rata billing credit of ₹100 per outage day after verification. You would be eligible for a credit of ₹200 for the two‑day outage.  

*Source: Refund Policy*", "latency_ms": 4143.64, "tokens_used": 572, "prompt_tokens": 276, "completion_tokens": 296}

